        "title": "Remove speculative merge retry reconciliation",
        "body": "Keep `merge_pr` focused on one concrete merge attempt.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nread target PR\n  \u2193\nverify required target/head state\n  \u2193\nrequest merge\n  \u2193\nreturn GitHub success or failure\n```\n\nDo not add special retry-success recognition for a hypothetical case where the merge succeeded but GitWeave did not receive the response.\n\nIf ambiguous merge completion becomes a demonstrated operational problem, solve that specific case later with the smallest necessary mechanism.\n\nRetain the explicit expected-head protection required by the merge contract.\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #54."
      }
